From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:27:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: honor DT firmware memory modes on PCI and AHB

ath12k selects the QCN9274 firmware memory mode from total system RAM.
That heuristic cannot describe embedded designs where a discrete radio has
to share memory and firmware resources with an integrated radio.

Allow a valid qcom,ath12k-fw-memory-mode property to select an existing
QMI memory mode, and use the same selector from the WiFi-7 AHB probe.
The AHB path previously ignored the property and always selected mode 0.

Preserve the fixed AHB default when the property is missing or invalid;
keep the RAM-based fallback for QCN9274 PCIe devices. This avoids changing
the default of other integrated radios without an explicit DT override.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1778,8 +1778,25 @@
 
 enum ath12k_qmi_mem_mode ath12k_core_get_memory_mode(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
+	u32 mode;
 	unsigned long total_ram;
 	struct sysinfo si;
+
+	if (!of_property_read_u32(ab->dev->of_node,
+				  "qcom,ath12k-fw-memory-mode", &mode)) {
+		if (mode <= ATH12K_QMI_MEMORY_MODE_LOW_512_M) {
+			ath12k_info(ab, "firmware memory mode %u from device tree\n",
+				    mode);
+			return (enum ath12k_qmi_mem_mode)mode;
+		}
+
+		ath12k_warn(ab, "ignoring unsupported firmware memory mode %u\n",
+			    mode);
+	}
+
+	/* Preserve the integrated-radio default without a valid DT override. */
+	if (ab->hif.bus == ATH12K_BUS_AHB)
+		return ATH12K_QMI_MEMORY_MODE_DEFAULT;
 
 	si_meminfo(&si);
 	total_ram = si.totalram * si.mem_unit;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ahb.c
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
 
-	ab->target_mem_mode = ATH12K_QMI_MEMORY_MODE_DEFAULT;
+	ab->target_mem_mode = ath12k_core_get_memory_mode(ab);
 	ab->hw_rev = hw_rev;
 
 	ret = ath12k_wifi7_hw_init(ab);
